WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.169
-President Trump
and his Attorney General

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.704
are turning
the Justice Department

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.006
into a political weapon
to protect Trump's friends

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.741
and punish his enemies,
and now Trump's

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.543
ex-Chief of Staff
is speaking out.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.578
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.180
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.849 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:20.019
-You might remember that in
order to justify their vote

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.854
to acquit Trump
in his impeachment trial,

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.456
several Republican Senators
tried to reassure us

00:00:24.456 --> 00:00:26.726
that impeachment would be
a teachable moment for Trump,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.261
that he would change
his behavior,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.829
and that he had learned
his lesson.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.031
-Enduring an impeachment
is something

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.466
that nobody should like.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.435
Even the president said he
didn't want that on his résumé.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.703
I don't blame him.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.540
So if a call like that
gets you an impeachment,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.642
I would think he would think
twice before he did it again.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.211
-I think that he knows now

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.181
that if he is trying
to do certain things,

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.249
whether it's ferreting
corruption there,

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.418
in Afghanistan, whatever it is,

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.455
he needs to go through
the proper channels.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.657
-Are you confident
that the president

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.827
won't seek foreign assistance
again?

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:05.631
-I believe that the president
has learned from this case.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.568
The president has been
impeached.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.870
That's a pretty big lesson.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.572
-You think he's learned
his lesson?

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.708
He's 73 years old and he hasn't
even learned

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.544
how to properly apply bronzer

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.845
all the way
to the top of his face.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.048
[ Laughter ]
I mean...

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.484
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.219
For real.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.855
Tom Hanks spent more time
putting makeup on Wilson.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.825
And sure enough,
within days of being acquitted,

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.827
Trump began a campaign
of exacting revenge

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.095
on impeachment witnesses

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.431
and proving that he had not
learned his lesson,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.066
as was obvious to all of us.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.202
For example,
he vindictively fired

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.769
Lieutenant Colonel
Alexander Vindman,

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:45.038
a key impeachment witness

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.240
who received a Purple Heart
for his service in Iraq.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.241
It was an on act
of petty revenge.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.410
And, yet, Trump defended
his firing of Vindman this week

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.413
by once again insisting
that the impeachable offense

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.181
he committed, his phone call
with the president of Ukraine,

00:01:56.181 --> 00:01:57.383
was actually perfect.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.351
-I obviously wasn't happy
with the job he did.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:01.387
First of all, he reported
a false call

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.922
that wasn't what was said
on the call.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.891
What was said on the call
was totally appropriate.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.125
And I call it a perfect call.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.694
I always will call it
a perfect call.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.062
-[ As Trump ]
It was a perfect call,

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.963
as perfect as my spray tan,

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:14.267
applied evenly
to every part of my face

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.002
so I definitely do not look like

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.537
an overcooked ham
with googly eyes."

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.838
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.406
[ Normal voice ] So now that
Trump is once again

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.341
abusing his power,
the Republicans who said

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.742
he learned his lesson
are silent.

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:26.846
But there was one Republican
who suddenly decided to speak up

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.214
at a paid speech yesterday,

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.149
and that's Trump's former
Chief of Staff John Kelly.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.584
Now, Kelly never spoke up

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.952
when he was Trump's
Chief of Staff

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.921
during some of Trump's worst
abuses and lowest moments.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.623
But now that he's getting paid
to give speeches,

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.525
John Kelly seems to have
grown a conscience

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.061
and now he's suddenly
criticizing Trump.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.263
-Former White House
Chief of Staff John Kelly

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.298
sounding off
on President Trump,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:47.966
as "The Atlantic" reports,

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:51.404
"The retired general explained
in the clearest terms yet

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.740
his misgivings with
Trump's behavior

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.643
regarding North Korea,
immigration, and Ukraine."

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.712
Speaking last night
at Drew University,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.480
Kelly said that,
"Lieutenant Colonel

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.218
Alexander Vindman was simply
following the training

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.053
he'd received as a soldier."

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:10.590
Kelly added, "We teach them,
'Don't follow an illegal order.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.625
If you're ever given one,
you'll raise it

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.728
with whoever gives it to you
and then you tell your boss.'"

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.630
-Hey, man, I'm going to say
the same thing to you

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.432
that I say about
the president's spray tan --

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.834
"Too little, too late."

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.503
And then after those comments
went public,

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.838
Kelly was rewarded for
his belated truth telling.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.673
The way anyone who turns
on Trump is rewarded

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.742
with a nasty personal attack
on Twitter.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.011
Trump tweeted
"When I terminated John Kelly,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.279
which I couldn't do fast enough,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.247
he knew full well that he was
way over his head,

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:37.350
being Chief of Staff
just wasn't for him.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.251
He came in with a bang,
went out with a whimper.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.787
But like so many exes,
he misses the action."

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:44.357
I'm sorry, do you mean the word,
exes?

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.193
It's not just spelled
with the letter "X."

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:50.429
When you say "X," people
tend to think of the X-Men.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.598
What X-Man would John Kelly be?

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.835
The one who waits a month
after Magneto destroys the city

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.237
and then says,
"We should have done something."

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.572
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.040
So now Trump is in a dumb feud

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.541
with one of his former
Chiefs of Staff.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:05.211
Meanwhile, we're learning
strange and new details

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.612
about his relationship
with another one

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.547
of his former Chiefs of Staff,
Reince Priebus,

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.883
and one particular
very dumb obsession

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.217
Trump had with Priebus.

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:14.720
Now as we all know, Donald Trump
is not a well-read man.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.388
But it's still fascinating
to find out the things

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.590
that he's curious about.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.291
This week, we learned
one of the strangest,

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:20.526
dumbest things about Trump yet

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.762
and it requires
a bit of explanation.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.496
Priebus was Trump's
first Chief of Staff.

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:26.832
And he was from Wisconsin,
which you may know,

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:28.334
is referred to
as the Badger State.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.736
And according to a new book
by the Trump administration

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:31.804
called "Sinking in the Swamp,"

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.039
Trump was obsessed with badgers

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:38.110
and he kept asking Priebus
questions about badgers,

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.546
even in situations where it
wasn't appropriate.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.282
These are real highlights
from the book.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:45.318
"When Reince Priebus was the
White House Chief of Staff,

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.919
President Donald Trump
repeatedly asked him

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.288
whether badgers, the state
animal of Priebus' home state

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:50.990
of Wisconsin,
are mean to people,

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.959
how they work,
and how aggressive they can get.

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:56.929
"Are they mean to people?" Trump
at least twice asked Priebus

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.564
in the opening months
of his presidency,

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.766
"or are they friendly
creatures?"

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:03.269
Trump also wanted to know
if the badger had a personality

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.570
or if it was boring,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.639
what kind of damage
could a badger do to a person

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.908
with its flashy, sharp claws?

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.710
Oh, my God,
Trump is obsessed with badgers.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.679
He's probably curious because
he can relate to the badger.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.082
I mean, look at him. He looks
like a mama badger fending off

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.484
a hoard of coyotes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.219
[ Applause ]

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.088
I mean, there's so many
questions about this.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.191
First of all, Trump want to know
how badgers work,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.792
like, what does he mean by work?

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.126
Does he mean,
"Do they have hearts

00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:29.628
that pump blood
to the rest of their bodies?"

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:32.364
or does he mean
"Do badgers have jobs?"

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:33.866
[ As Trump ] So what do these
badgers do for a living?

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.534
Do they build dams like beavers?

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.204
You know, 'cause I'm --
I'm in real estate, too."

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.638
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.073
[ Normal voice ] Seriously think
about how insane this is.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:42.541
The president
of the United States

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:45.144
has shown more genuine curiosity
about badgers and how they work

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.579
than literally any other subject
in his portfolio.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:50.015
He's 70 going on 7.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.984
Was he asked
for environmental reasons,

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.953
or for his second-grade essay
project?

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.254
[ As Trump, monotone ]
This summer, I learned

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.723
how badgers work and if they
are mean to people.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.992
They have personalities
and are not boring and stupid

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.694
like my ex, John Kelly."

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:06.198
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Normal voice ] In fact,

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.000
according to the book,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.302
Trump showed more genuine
curiosity about badgers

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:11.637
than actual policy issues.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.040
For example, just this week
he intervened directly

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.675
into the criminal case of one
of his cronies, Roger Stone,

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:18.611
seen here dressed like
a Bond villain,

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:22.614
who instead of petting a white
cat pets a Wisconsin badger.

00:06:22.614 --> 00:06:24.083
Stone was convicted of lying
to Congress

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.619
and witness tampering to help
cover up the Russia conspiracy

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.587
as part of Robert Mueller's
investigation.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.723
Prosecutors originally
recommended up to nine years

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.225
in jail, but then Trump
whined about how unfair it was

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.960
on Twitter,
and his Justice Department,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.528
led by Attorney General
Bill Barr

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:39.298
intervened to change it to
a much more lenient sentence.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.300
And yesterday Trump
celebrated that move

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.735
claiming no one could even
specify

00:06:43.735 --> 00:06:45.037
what Stone was guilty of.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.005
-I want to thank
the Justice Department

00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:49.708
for seeing this horrible thing.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.712
They saw the horribleness
of a nine-year sentence

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:53.846
for doing nothing.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.614
Nine years for doing something

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:57.883
that nobody even can define
what he did.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.718
-Just because you
can't define it,

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:01.787
doesn't mean nobody
can define it.

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:03.489
I mean, you can ask your lawyer.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.525
he should at least
be able to look it up.

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.593
I mean, he's always
showing us his phone.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.528
[ As Giuliani ] Boss, again,
I Googled "witness tampering,"

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.797
and it says right here,
apply ointment as necessary,

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.567
then use a cooling pad --
Oh, sorry, wrong tab.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:17.103
I also Googled "what to do when
you sit on your own balls."

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.739
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:22.541
[ Normal voice ] What's clear
here is that Trump and Barr

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:24.543
are turning the
Justice Department into a tool

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:26.312
for Trump's personal political
benefit.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.280
In fact, Barr is taking
control of cases

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.349
that are of personal interest
to Trump

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.417
and has reportedly even made
himself

00:07:32.417 --> 00:07:34.019
into Trump's personal defender.

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:36.388
-Barr describing
an expansive new profile

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.524
in "The New Yorker" as
attempting to maximize

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.360
executive power, and,
"Like no Attorney General

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.828
since the Watergate era,

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.464
he has acted as the president's
political sword and shield."

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:47.833
-That's right, Barr is now
Trump's sword and shield,

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.268
which is true metaphorically.

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:52.271
But you know Trump would also
love a literal sword and shield.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:54.340
I'm surprised that they don't
just let him walk around

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.242
the White House with a sword
from Medieval Times

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:58.944
and a Burger King crown
so he can yell

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:01.047
[ As Trump ]
Where are you, badgers?!

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:04.950
Don't try to charm me with
your winning personality.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.519
[ Normal voice ] And if it seems
to you like Barr is acting

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.421
more like Trump's
personal defense attorney

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:10.022
than the Attorney General of the
United States,

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.224
just remember at
his confirmation hearing

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:15.428
last year, Barr revealed
that he literally did interview

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:16.762
to become Trump's
defense attorney

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.130
during the Mueller investigation

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.366
before Trump appointed him
Attorney General.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:25.304
-It was a very brief meeting
where essentially the president

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:28.173
wanted to know -- Yeah, he said,
"Oh, you know Bob Mueller.

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:29.441
How well do you know Bob
Mueller?

00:08:29.441 --> 00:08:31.677
I told him how well I knew
Bob Mueller,

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:35.514
and he was interested in that,
wanted to know what I thought

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:38.250
about Mueller's integrity
and so forth and so on.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.285
So he asked me
for my phone number.

00:08:40.285 --> 00:08:43.088
I gave it to him, and I never
heard from him again.

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.090
-I mean, I know why
he never called you.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.926
He was probably distracted by
some dumb thought about animals

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:50.129
that had nothing to do with
what you were talking about.

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:51.297
Trump was probably sitting there

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.664
while you were talking
thinking to himself,

00:08:52.664 --> 00:08:54.433
[ As Trump ] I wonder which
animals are nice

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.969
and which ones are mean.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:09:00.105
I bet squirrels are nice
and pigeons are mean.

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:03.475
Elephants are nice,
Bobcats are mean.

00:09:03.475 --> 00:09:04.510
Groundhogs are neutral.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.011
No one ever had a problem
with groundhogs.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:09.315
Oh, and penguins are fancy
because they wear tuxedos!

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:10.816
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.351
[ Normal voice ] So an imbecile
President whose only interest

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:15.120
in his own self-preservation is
turning the Justice Department

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.988
into a political weapon
for his own benefit,

00:09:16.988 --> 00:09:19.024
Trump keeps digging himself
deeper and deeper,

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:22.861
much like Trump's great friend,
the majestic badger,

00:09:22.861 --> 00:09:24.363
whose mating call echoes

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.864
throughout the forests
of Wisconsin.

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:28.100
And I imagine if Trump
were to hear that call,

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.435
he might say something like...

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:30.669
-They call it a perfect call.

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.304
I always will call it
a perfect call.

00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:33.772
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:35.207
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:37.209 line:0%
♪♪

